[1m[38;5;231mWhich forms are planned, and what kinds of rules do they need beyond "required"?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] Required only
  [38;5;246mSame as today, just per-field and not hardcoded. Smallest possible shared layer.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Required + format
  [38;5;246mRequired, plus built-in formats like email, min/max length, numeric range, pattern match.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] + Cross-field rules
  [38;5;246mRules that compare fields — password confirmation, date ranges, "one of these is required".[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] + Async rules
  [38;5;246mRules needing a server round-trip, e.g. "is this username taken". This materially changes the interface (everything [39m
  [38;5;246mbecomes promise-based).[39m
